===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|dette||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʰeh₁bʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|dette}}, {{m|enm|dett}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|dete}} ({{cog|fr|dette}}), from {{der|en|ML.|dēbita}}, from {{der|en|la|dēbitum||what is owed, a debt, a duty}}, neuter of {{m|la|dēbitus}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|dēbeō||I owe}}, contraction of {{m|la|*dehibeō||I have from}}, from {{m|la|de||from}} + {{m|la|habeō||I have}}. {{doublet|en|debit}}.

The unpronounced "b" in the modern English spelling is a [[Latinisation]] from the Latin etymon {{m|la|dēbitum}}.

